Commit:     Guillaume de Rouville <guillaume@dagger.io>
CommitDate: Sat Sep 26 23:11:16 2026 -0700

    perf: defer custom Go bases through an explicit Address
    
    Add optional baseAddress after existing constructor arguments. Retain the
    caller-bound Address until GoModule.base needs its Container; discovery can
    list modules and tests without invoking an execution-only base producer.
    Keep base: Container eager, reject both options together, and preserve
    custom-toolchain version warnings and ordinary parent function caching.
    
    Workspace settings use baseAddress (camelCase) instead of base and require
    the engine Address-default correction dagger/dagger commit 36e4939021.
    Producer/type errors for the opt-in address surface when the base is used.
    
    Add GoDev checks for non-consumption, constructor policy, error propagation,
    custom environment/files, a live bound service, tests and generation. The
    existing Container-base check also passes. Pin these QA fixture images to
    the tested digests. Three targeted checks ran on the diagnostic engine;
    the entire GoDev suite and additional platforms were not run. Final source
    only changes the version description and canonical formatting after testing.
    
    Matched local listings on the experimental SDK stack measured warm
    1.392 -> 1.138s and new-comment edits 1.409 -> 1.106s (four samples per arm).
    Four fresh-volume observations were 25.533/29.421s versus21.142/20.918s;
    host caches were retained and disk variation remains. No Cloud or check
    execution speedup is claimed. Full evidence lives in grouville/dagger's
    perf/collections-discovery branch under hack/collections-qa-performance-data.
    
    Further work: remove remaining pure-helper runtime round trips, measure
    catalog readiness before changing scheduling, and preserve workspace
    binding/cache policy when extending this pattern to other modules.

